      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "It is impossible to treat all varicose veins employing the same method. Cryosurgery offers a new modality for the detraction of the long and short saphenous vein deletion."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To describe the technique, its indications, potential complications, and cosmetic results."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "We followed 800 patients over 6 years. The study allows evaluation of the results of and the best indications for this method. With a follow up of five years, we have analyzed: 1) the immediate complications, and 2) middle-term results."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The results of cryosurgery of varicose veins were generally comparable to those obtained using classical surgery (stripping)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Cryosurgery of varicose veins is a fast and safe method for selected varicose disorders, exhibiting good cosmetic results."
        }
      ]},
